KaiT2en-NixOS divergence: the DSP sink is the only internal speaker device.

Upstream's speaker graphs play into the UCM split-PCM node and leave it
selectable, so a stream routed there reaches the transducers with no
crossover and no limiter. With the companion UCM patch
(apple-t2-alsa-ucm-conf-speaker-direct.patch) the Speaker device is a
plain hw:${CardId},0 node; this gives that node the name and channel
layout its graph targets, marks it Audio/Sink/Internal, hides the card's
"[Out] Speaker" port from desktop sound panels (api.acp.hidden-ports),
and names the DSP sink after the machine family ("MacBook Pro
Speakers"). Tests assert that every model's layout and target name match
its graph. (Originally landed in-tree as fe14b8f and 3811916; moved here
in the 2026-11-15 sync so dsp/ stays byte-identical to upstream.)

Applied by dsp/package.nix on top of the upstream source (-p1 relative
to dsp/), together with the UCM patch: either one alone breaks the
speaker path.

Drop condition: remove (with the UCM patch) when upstream's dsp/ makes
the DSP sink the only selectable internal speaker device -- the raw
speaker node hidden from both the sink list and the card's ports.
Re-check every sync.

